Heli builder using buildVehicleModel:
```
function makeAmbientHeli(city, x,z, radius, height, speed, color){
 const model = buildVehicleModel('helicopter', color, {});
 const group=model.group; group.scale.setScalar(.85); city.root.add(group);
 const a={ group, rotor:model.rotor, tailRotor:model.tailRotor, angle: Math.random()*TAU, radius, height, speed, x,z, update(dt,t){
   this.angle += this.speed*dt;
   const px=this.x+Math.cos(this.angle)*this.radius;
   const pz=this.z+Math.sin(this.angle)*this.radius;
   group.position.set(px, this.height + Math.sin(t*.6+this.angle)*2.2, pz);
   const heading=Math.atan2(-Math.sin(this.angle), Math.cos(this.angle)); // tangent derivative dx=-sin, dz=cos
   group.rotation.y=heading;
   group.rotation.z = -.12; // bank
   group.rotation.x = 0;
   this.rotor.rotation.y += dt*40; tailRotor.rotation.x += dt*56;
 }}
}
```
Actually derivative of (cos, sin) is (-sin, cos) → heading atan2(dx,dz)=atan2(-sin,cos). Good.

Helis at (0,55,0) radius 200 and (200,45,50) radius 120. One should land: implement a "helipad shuttle":
```
const heli group at helipad (city.helipad)
a={ mode:'land'...}
```
But perhaps circling is enough. The user said helicopter and planes that have flown or land on. Add a heli that periodically lands on hospital helipad: state machine:
- cycle 50s: 0-10 takeoff from helipad and climb, 10-30 circle radius 90 around helipad at y 45, 30-40 return and descend, 40-50 parked.
This is more work. Alternatively use path aircraft for heli with vertical waypoints including ground at helipad, but path needs smooth takeoff. We can use the same path flyer at slow speed with points:
```
path = [
 {x:hx, z:hz, y:.6}, {x:hx, z:hz, y:38}, {x:hx+60,z:hz+60,y:55}, ... circle ... return {x:hx,z:hz,y:.6}
]
```
If path is closed, it will repeat landing/takeoff. The model pitch from vertical segments would be extreme; clamp pitch and smooth. Bank on turns. That's acceptable and looks like a heli taking off/landing. Use speed 14, path with points around helipad.

But path flyer sets rotation.x from y difference; for vertical takeoff segment dir.x,z ~0, pitch = atan2(-dy, 0)= -90°, bad. Clamp pitch to ±0.35. Fine.

Direction yaw when horizontal distance 0: use previous yaw. Add guard.

Let's implement makePathAircraft generic with clamp pitch and heading fallback.

Airliner path as designed. Ambient high plane circle: use path with 8 waypoints at y=210 around radius 650.

Also runway edge lights: add small emissive dots along both sides at x=cx+60±22 every 15. Nice at night. Instanced maybe; keep simple loop 40 meshes but merged static. Add.

Also add approach lights.

