Now update `updateRidingCamera`. Need trainLen and target middle. Also ensure when riding the island rail, `r` has group and trainLength userData.

Implementation:
```
updateRidingCamera(dt) {
  const r=this.riding;
  const cam=this.camera;
  const t=r.group ? r.group.position : r.pos;
  const trainHeading = r.group?.rotation.y ?? this.cameraYaw;
  if (this.lookHold>0) this.lookHold-=dt; else this.cameraYaw=lerpAngle(...);
  const yaw=this.cameraYaw;
  const cars=r.group?.userData?.cars;
  const trainLen = r.group?.userData?.trainLength ?? (cars?.length ? (cars.length-1)*10.6+10 : 22);
  const forward = new THREE.Vector3(Math.sin(trainHeading),0,Math.cos(trainHeading));
  const mid = new THREE.Vector3(t.x - forward.x*(trainLen*.5-5), t.y+2, t.z - forward.z*(trainLen*.5-5));
  if (firstPerson) { eye = t + forward*2.2 ...; }
  const dist = (this.cameraDist||18) + trainLen*.55;
  back using yaw...
}
```
Wait, sign: forward = local +z rotated. Cars extend local -z, so tail = t - forward*(len). Mid = t - forward*(len/2 - 5). Yes.

First-person: at front car interior: eye = t + forward*2.0 (since nose local +z at t). Looking along forward. Good.

The `back` vector: camera behind the mid relative to yaw, at distance. If yaw==trainHeading, camera behind. Good.

Set desired y:
```
const desired = new THREE.Vector3(mid.x + back.x*dist, mid.y + 4.5 + Math.sin(cameraPitch)*dist*.6, mid.z + back.z*dist)
```
Actually mid.y already t.y+2. Add ~4. Use Math.max.

Let's implement.

input.newString:
updateRidingCamera(dt) {
  const r = this.riding;
  const cam = this.camera;
  const t = r.group ? r.group.position : r.pos;
  const trainHeading = r.group?.rotation.y ?? this.cameraYaw;
  if (this.lookHold > 0) this.lookHold -= dt;
  else this.cameraYaw = lerpAngle(this.cameraYaw, trainHeading, clamp(dt * 2.2, 0, 1));
  const yaw = this.cameraYaw;
  // The train geometry grows backwards along its local -Z axis, so aim at
  // the middle of the consist rather than the lead car's origin.
  const cars = r.group?.userData?.cars;
  const trainLen = r.group?.userData?.trainLength ?? (cars?.length ? (cars.length - 1) * 10.6 + 10 : 22);
  const fx = Math.sin(trainHeading), fz = Math.cos(trainHeading);
  if (this.firstPerson) {
    const eye = new THREE.Vector3(t.x + fx * 1.8, t.y + 2.3, t.z + fz * 1.8);
    cam.position.lerp(eye, clamp(dt * 8, 0, 1));
    cam.lookAt(eye.x + fx * 30, eye.y - .25 + Math.sin(this.cameraPitch) * 14, eye.z + fz * 30);
    return;
  }
  const mid = new THREE.Vector3(
    t.x - fx * (trainLen * .5 - 5),
    t.y + 2.1,
    t.z - fz * (trainLen * .5 - 5)
  );
  const dist = (this.cameraDist || 18) + trainLen * .55;
  const back = new THREE.Vector3(-Math.sin(yaw), 0, -Math.cos(yaw)).multiplyScalar(dist);
  const desired = new THREE.Vector3(
    mid.x + back.x,
    mid.y + 4.4 + Math.sin(this.cameraPitch) * dist * .55,
    mid.z + back.z
  );
  cam.position.lerp(desired, clamp(dt * 4, 0, 1));
  cam.lookAt(mid);
}

